{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790009490,"nonce":"1y3McVBQM7/mxQMuO831SVbbOw8=","message":"Changed 2026-09-21: this repo dogfoods the `jira` preset, not `linear`.\n\nThe original reasoning was 'no Jira here, so run linear'. It points the wrong way: with the sandbox skipped (de1d8fb), the jira preset is written from REST API documentation and verified by nothing. Dogfooding it means it is exercised every day against real issues, which is the only check it will get before it meets the company instance. The linear preset stays in the round-trip table test, which is where it earns its keep.\n\nConsequence for bf6f392: our labels migrate onto Jira's model, and one mapping needs a call — type:decision has no native Jira issue type. Either add a custom type to the preset, or map decisions to Task and keep a marker. Worth noting area: maps naturally onto Components, which is a multi-enum, so the migration exercises that kind too.","files":null}]}